WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.669
-Welcome back.
I'm talking to Dwayne Johnson,

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.604
whose new NBC series,
"Young Rock,"

00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:07.507
premieres February 16th,
at 8:00 p.m.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.241
And joining us right now --
I'm very lucky --

00:00:09.241 --> 00:00:12.779
is one of the actors from
the series, Bradley Constant.

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:15.648
Bradley, there you are.

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:18.317
Thank you so much
for coming on, bud.

00:00:18.317 --> 00:00:20.987
You play young Rock.

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.689
You play Dwayne Johnson
at 15 years old.

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:25.692
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.
-Do you know --

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.193
I mean, you must have heard
some of the stories.

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:30.129
But I know from some of the
stories I've heard from Dwayne,

00:00:30.129 --> 00:00:33.600
15, he's lived
a pretty crazy life.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.801
I mean, he was getting arrested.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.902
I mean, he's constantly
moving around.

00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:42.375
I mean, crazy stories that you
don't -- you have no idea.

00:00:42.375 --> 00:00:43.709
-Yeah.
-Dwayne, you remember

00:00:43.709 --> 00:00:45.077
there was that one --

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:47.280
kids thought you were
an undercover cop?

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:50.383
-Yes. When we were evicted
from Hawaii,

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:54.286
we were forced
to live, or go to, Nashville.

00:00:54.286 --> 00:00:56.322
So, when I went to Nashville --

00:00:56.322 --> 00:01:00.193
In the state of Hawaii,
you can get your license at 14,

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:02.562
or at least you could back then,
when I was a kid.

00:01:02.562 --> 00:01:06.833
And so I show up in Nashville,
driving a car,

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:12.271
full, full moustache,
6'4", 220 pounds.

00:01:12.271 --> 00:01:14.340
The kids were in --
You know, I looked

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.911
not like too many people running
around Nashville at that time.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.480
So, "21 Jump Street"
was a popular TV show

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.914
that was happening at that time.

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:23.916
Oh, for sure, they were like...
-You're a narc.

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:25.718
-..."This is the real life --
We have the real-life

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:28.721
'21 Jump Street' happening
in our school right now."

00:01:28.721 --> 00:01:32.659
And Bradley has the opportunity,
and he crushed it,

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:36.562
of playing me at 15,
that undercover-cop time.

00:01:36.562 --> 00:01:41.968
-Bradley, are -- are you -- were
you ready to take on that role?

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.803
-Man, I was -- I was pumped.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:45.972
I was extremely excited, yeah.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:48.241
-Dwayne, we have a photo of you
at 15 years old.

00:01:48.241 --> 00:01:50.276
What do you remember
about this guy?

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.812
-Oh, God.
Don't do it.

00:01:52.812 --> 00:01:54.413
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.413 --> 00:01:57.750
-Wow! That's 15?
-That's 15.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.586
And I'm clearly aggressive.

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:02.788
And I loved boom boxes.

00:02:02.788 --> 00:02:05.090
And, you know,
that was at the time

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:06.225
where I was getting in trouble,

00:02:06.225 --> 00:02:07.526
trying to stay
on the right path.

00:02:07.526 --> 00:02:10.429
And, you know, Bradley,
as you can see now,

00:02:10.429 --> 00:02:13.232
has just such
a great personality.

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:16.736
And he's so funny and charming,
and he's a tremendous actor.

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:19.305
Even though our show
is a comedy, you know,

00:02:19.305 --> 00:02:21.440
he's got to step into
those 15-year-old shoes

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:23.542
where I was a complicated kid

00:02:23.542 --> 00:02:24.944
who was getting
in trouble a lot.

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:27.847
But -- But also --
And this is what I shared

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.382
with Bradley is, man,
I was getting in trouble,

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:32.385
I was getting arrested, I was --

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.754
We got evicted,
I was angry that we got evicted,

00:02:34.754 --> 00:02:37.357
I was angry that we were living
paycheck to paycheck.

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:39.125
And I said, "But, Bradley,"
I said,

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:42.495
"If you can find
that little voice

00:02:42.495 --> 00:02:44.396
and little thing inside you

00:02:44.396 --> 00:02:46.866
that allows you still
to be a good kid."

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.868
And I said, "You know,
because I was still

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:50.303
a good kid at that time.

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:51.804
I think he really,
really crushed it.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:55.908
-Here's a photo of me
at 15 or 14.

00:02:55.908 --> 00:02:57.844
That's me.
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:57.844 --> 00:02:59.979
-Is that is a mullet?
Is that is a mullet?

00:02:59.979 --> 00:03:01.681
-Yeah, it was --
-It is a mullet! Wait a second.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:03.649
-It's kind of being a mullet
a little bit.

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:05.051
It's a lot going on.

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:06.819
I don't know what
hairstyle that is.

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:08.121
-And look how happy you are.
Wait a second.

00:03:08.121 --> 00:03:09.888
Are you --
Is this karaoke time?

00:03:09.888 --> 00:03:12.325
-This is my house.
We had --

00:03:12.325 --> 00:03:15.060
My dad fixed some jukebox
someone was throwing out.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:19.298
I was doing -- either singing or
doing stand-up or something.

00:03:19.298 --> 00:03:21.301
And it looks like there's a
pizza-delivery guy at the house.

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:23.635
I don't know why --
who that man is

00:03:23.635 --> 00:03:25.104
with the red shirt
and white pants.

00:03:25.104 --> 00:03:27.539
[ Laughter ]
But odd.

00:03:27.539 --> 00:03:29.976
Anyway, that was a Friday night
at the Fallon house.

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:31.777
I was probably
doing something ridiculous.

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:34.614
But I was --
Oh, that's me --

00:03:34.614 --> 00:03:36.115
All right, we can stop
with the photos now.

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:38.784
This is just --
-Wait, wait, are you going --

00:03:38.784 --> 00:03:42.555
Are you going to school?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:43.890
-That is not
a Halloween costume.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:46.191
That is actually
what I wore to work.

00:03:46.191 --> 00:03:49.329
I got a job --
I got a job as soon as I could.

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:50.796
I can't believe
they had that photo.

00:03:50.796 --> 00:03:52.365
Gosh.
-What were you doing?

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:54.334
Were you at a pizza joint?
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:54.334 --> 00:03:56.569
-I was an old -- looks like
I was an old-timey bartender.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:03:58.670
I don't know what I was doing.
That was a --

00:03:58.670 --> 00:03:59.838
-Ice-cream parlor or something.

00:03:59.838 --> 00:04:02.274
-No, I was a bag boy
at a grocery store.

00:04:02.274 --> 00:04:04.710
I was the best.
Uh, yeah.

00:04:04.710 --> 00:04:06.411
If you --
People would request --

00:04:06.411 --> 00:04:09.515
They would request me.
They're like, "Get me Jimmy."

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:11.684
I was fast,
and I would put eggs on top.

00:04:11.684 --> 00:04:13.986
I knew how to do it, man.
-That was my first --

00:04:13.986 --> 00:04:16.189
one of my first jobs, too.
I worked at a grocery store.

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:18.590
-Did you really?
-Up until last year,

00:04:18.590 --> 00:04:19.758
when I booked this, yeah.

00:04:19.758 --> 00:04:22.027
-Bradley, where's your
15-year-old photo?

00:04:22.027 --> 00:04:23.295
-Oh, goodness.
-Didn't we drag one

00:04:23.295 --> 00:04:26.432
out of Bradley's --
Yeah, ooh!

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:28.500
-[ Laughs ]
-What's this guy?

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.336
What's this bit?
-All right.

00:04:30.336 --> 00:04:33.339
Look. Okay.
So, 15-year-old Bradley.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:36.009
I was --
I think I was trying to say,

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:38.044
"Hey, I don't have money,
so don't ask me,"

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:40.413
so I had empty pockets
and everything.

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.748
I was like, "Don't bother me."
I don't know.

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:43.416
-Wait.
That's your bit is to come in

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:44.984
with your pockets hanging out?

00:04:44.984 --> 00:04:48.120
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.689
-I don't know.
I felt really cool

00:04:49.689 --> 00:04:50.856
with that sweater, man.

00:04:50.856 --> 00:04:53.592
Bamm-Bamm with a
Louisville slugger, come on.

00:04:53.592 --> 00:04:54.860
-Let me see that.

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:56.295
That's not even, like,
the real --

00:04:56.295 --> 00:04:59.465
Bamm-Bamm had white hair
or blond hair.

00:04:59.465 --> 00:05:01.801
-Look.
-Yeah, that's like Blam-Blam.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:03.836
-That's like Boom-Boom.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:07.040
-Boom-Boom.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.309
-That's fake Bamm-Bamm.
Oh, my gosh.

00:05:10.309 --> 00:05:11.977
Bradley, when you
come on my show,

00:05:11.977 --> 00:05:14.012
'cause I'm telling you
right now, dude,

00:05:14.012 --> 00:05:15.781
when you come on my show,
'cause I'm telling you,

00:05:15.781 --> 00:05:17.416
I think you're gonna be
nominated for an Emmy one day,

00:05:17.416 --> 00:05:19.919
and when you do,
you come on my show,

00:05:19.919 --> 00:05:21.320
and you have to have
the pockets out

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.289
and the Bamm-Bamm sweatshirt.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.289 --> 00:05:25.858
-I got it.

00:05:25.858 --> 00:05:27.393
Don't ask me for money
'cause I won't have it.

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.662
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.662 --> 00:05:30.829
-Congrats on everything.

00:05:30.829 --> 00:05:32.298
I want to show a clip
of the show.

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:35.167
Here's a look at the premiere
episode of "Young Rock."

00:05:35.167 --> 00:05:37.537
Take a look at this, everybody.

00:05:37.537 --> 00:05:41.840
-Anyway, best part is, Karen
invited me to a party tonight.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:43.776
So, life is good, huh?
-It is.

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:46.545
-Well, it's not gonna last.
Fine-ass Karen aside,

00:05:46.545 --> 00:05:48.314
the reason why these girls
haven't been giving you

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:50.516
the time of day
isn't 'cause you look poor.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:52.518
It's 'cause you look like
an undercover cop,

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:54.486
like Johnny Depp
from "21 Jump Street."

00:05:54.486 --> 00:05:55.754
-No one thinks that.

00:05:55.754 --> 00:05:58.491
-Dwayne, everyone thinks that.

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.527
-[ Whispering ]
He's looking at me.

00:06:01.527 --> 00:06:03.662
He's a cop, like Johnny Depp.

00:06:03.662 --> 00:06:05.598
-I'm 15!

00:06:05.598 --> 00:06:08.400
-You have a full moustache,
and you're bigger than a dad.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.369
You look like you work
at an auto-parts store.

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:11.670
-Whatever, man.

00:06:11.670 --> 00:06:13.872
None of that matters
now that I got a girl into me.

00:06:13.872 --> 00:06:17.443
-Yeah, but that girl thinks
you're rich, and you're not.

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:19.512
-Dwayne Johnson
and Bradley Constant.

00:06:19.512 --> 00:06:22.247
"Young Rock" premiere
February 16th

00:06:22.247 --> 00:06:24.717
at 8:00 p.m., on NBC.

00:06:24.717 --> 00:06:28.053
Daniel Kaluuya joins us
when we come back.

00:06:28.053 --> 00:06:30.223
Thanks so much, guys.
I appreciate it.

